# PR hygiene

- Keep pull requests small and scoped. Do not mix an unrelated refactor with a signal change.
- Use the pull request template. Fill in schema diff, golden-eval results, and the cost estimate. Leave any of those sections as "none" with a reason rather than deleting them.
- Do not merge your own pull request. Builder and the cloud agent never merge and never deploy to production.
- Do not commit generated warehouse files, `.env`, API keys, or Snowflake tokens.
- Schema changes are additive inside `signals` (DuckDB) or `MCP_DB.SIGNAL_SANDBOX` (Snowflake). Call out every new column in the schema diff.
